  "structuring": {
    "prompt_variant": null,
    "prompt_additions": "UAE federal legislation uses ARTICLE as the basic unit (مادة, maddah), not SECTION. The hierarchy is: BOOK (codes only) > PART > CHAPTER > ARTICLE > SUBSECTION (numbered clauses) > PARAGRAPH (lettered sub-clauses). Article numbering is continuous throughout the law regardless of Chapter/Part boundaries. Headings after the ARTICLE number are the article title. DIFC and ADGM laws use SECTION as the basic unit and follow Anglophone structure.",
    "rtl_script": true,
    "rtl_note": "Arabic source documents are right-to-left. The OCR pipeline must handle Arabic bidi text. Structural keywords in the Arabic source will be in Arabic script; English translations use the English keywords listed above."
  },
